      "content": "TL 10 NW                    REDBOURN             HOGG END LANE                                                  (south side) 9/220                                            Butler's Farmhouse                                                  (including front garden                                                  wall) II Farmhouse.  Circa 1700, altered c.1830.  Square red brick house with plain tile hipped roof.  2 storeys.  3 large sash windows with segmental heads.   2 ridge chimney stacks, the left one broader and from original house.  Right side has cellar;  blocked windows  on  right  elevation.   Interior  with  c.1830  detail. Attached to front of house is C17-origin red brick and flint garden wall with C19 brick coping;  square plan. Listing NGR: TL1121908729"
    }
